\item[* task:] Insert a cliticnode. In this cliticnode all the clitics will be 
inserted as daughters.  
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)\\
In this way we are able to control the order of the 
clitics and it is possible to move the whole node to another place after the 
time rules (clustering of auxiliaries) and substitution rules. As canonical 
place the place inmediately after the main verb is chosen. If the cliticnode 
remains empty it has to be deleted after the substitution rules.
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:] The reason for 
inserting it here always and not only when it is necessary, is because in that 
case there are always two possibilities for every rule concerning clitics: 1) 
there is already a CLITIC node present and 2) there is no CLITIC node present 
yet.
